#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Where Alph
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
#> must: 3
#> not: measureless
#> not: sunless
#> source: 3q
# 20. = writes the line number; q stops. McMahon 3.7
# = writes the current line number on a line of its own, immediately. q writes
# the current line (unless -n), flushes any appended text, and ends: nothing
# after line 3 is even read, which is what makes "sed 10q" a cheap head.
# The paper ends here; the sed you have has grown (GNU extensions: -E, -i, y,
# first~step...). Tutorials 2 and 3 cover the one-liners and the cheat sheet.
# Try: #ARGS -n with $= alone counts the lines, as wc -l does.
=
3q

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
